bluuur 2.0.0 is a modified version of Mac Duo 0.1.0-dev.18.1.
Upstream: https://github.com/sumimakito/Mac-Duo
Base commit: 2a9fa18bea0e92293bf59227b539fe3de0e91328
Changes: bluuur branding and bundle identity, Russian localization, a settings
window available on launch/reopen, and optional mouse-friendly perspective.
Original GPU renderer, blur, live stream, sensor, and lid animation retained.
The original author does not endorse this modified version.

Changes in bluuur 2.0.1: hold the visual spring flat until capture is ready,
reveal after the first submitted render, and ease perspective restoration
after mouse use. The steady-state effect remains the Mac Duo effect.

Changes in bluuur 2.0.2: a centred Gaussian pyramid fixes blur drifting right;
the upstream footer is removed from the settings UI. Copyright and licensing
notices remain in this distribution.

Changes in bluuur 2.0.3: reachable start-angle calibration, exact critically
damped animation, immediate live-stream startup, delayed screenshot fallback,
and retry for a missing first picture.
Further 2.0.3 fixes: recover failed stream enumeration and unexpected stream
stops, reject self-capture when exclusion is unavailable, apply picture mode
changes immediately, bound queued GPU frames, and validate HID report length.
Settings now rise above the effect only while bluuur is active and authorized,
and return to normal level when another app or a system prompt takes focus.

Changes in bluuur 2.0.4: a persistent dark settings appearance in both the
window and menu-bar popover, graphite background, blue control accent, and
more legible explanatory text. The effect and saved settings are unchanged.

Changes in bluuur 2.0.5: near-black settings background and window title bar;
white control tint replaces the blue accent. Effect behavior is unchanged.

Changes in bluuur 2.0.6: slight settings-window translucency; user-facing
installer naming and instructions omit the version number. Effect unchanged.

Changes in bluuur 2.0.7: consistent product naming in all permission-message
translations; download image includes the app and Applications shortcut only.
License and attribution notices are retained inside the app bundle.
